<section id="terms" lang="en">
  <h2>Terms of Service (English)</h2>
  <p class="muted"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 18 October 2026</p>
  <p>These terms apply when you use Thaqib, made by Lunabit Labs.</p>
  <h3>Agreeing to these terms</h3>
  <p>By using Thaqib, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the app. Thaqib from the App Store is also covered by Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a>.</p>
  <h3>What Thaqib is</h3>
  <p>Thaqib helps families encourage good habits: kids check in when they've done something good, a grown-up approves, and stars add up to rewards the family chooses.</p>
  <h3>The Thaqib Family subscription</h3>
  <p>Thaqib Family is an auto-renewable subscription. It unlocks Thaqib for the whole family: up to 4 grown-ups and 6 kids, on any device, whichever Apple Account it uses. Shared iPads are free.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Price and length: the yearly price is shown in the app before you buy, in your own currency. Payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase, or when a free month ends.</li>
    <li>Free month: new subscribers may start with one month free. Unless it's cancelled at least 24 hours before the month ends, the yearly subscription begins and is charged.</li>
    <li>Renewal: the subscription renews each year unless it's cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current year. The renewal is charged within the 24 hours before that.</li>
    <li>Cancelling: in the Settings app, tap your name, then Subscriptions; or in Thaqib, Settings › Subscription › Manage in the App Store. The subscription then runs until the end of the period already paid for.</li>
    <li>Family Sharing: Thaqib Family can be shared with your Apple family.</li>
    <li>When it ends: Thaqib rests. Nothing is deleted; the kids still see their stars and their sky, and check-ins, approvals and rewards wait until someone in the family subscribes again.</li>
    <li>Founding families: if you bought Thaqib before it became a subscription, your family keeps everything, free, for good.</li>
    <li>Refunds are handled by Apple, under its own terms.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Families and supervision</h3>
  <p>A parent or guardian sets up the family and is responsible for how Thaqib is used with their children, including who is invited, what is rewarded, and keeping the family PIN private. Rewards come from your family; we don't provide or fulfil them.</p>
  <h3>Religious content</h3>
  <p>The deeds Thaqib suggests for Prayers, Quran and Character &amp; manners support your family's practice; they aren't religious rulings. Thaqib doesn't calculate prayer times. For religious guidance, consult a qualified scholar.</p>
  <h3>Your information</h3>
  <p>Your family's information is kept on your devices and in your iCloud, as the <a href="/thaqib/privacy/#privacy">Privacy Policy</a> describes. Sharing a family between devices uses your Apple Account and iCloud, which Apple provides under its own terms.</p>
  <h3>Ownership</h3>
  <p>Thaqib, its design and its content belong to Lunabit Labs and are protected by copyright and other laws.</p>
  <h3>No warranty</h3>
  <p>Thaqib is provided “as is”, without warranties of any kind. We don't promise it will always be available or free of errors.</p>
  <h3>Limitation of liability</h3>
  <p>As far as the law allows, Lunabit Labs isn't liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of Thaqib.</p>
  <h3>Changes</h3>
  <p>We may update these terms. The new version will be in the app and on this page, with its date at the top, and using Thaqib after a change means you accept it.</p>
  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Write to <a href="mailto:support@luna.bh">support@luna.bh</a>.</p>
</section>
